+## Pausing and resuming subscriptions
+
+Each subscription has an **enabled** toggle in the subscriptions list and on its detail view. Turning it off pauses delivery without deleting the subscription or losing its configuration – turn it back on to resume on the next scheduled delivery.
+
+If a subscription's delivery target becomes permanently invalid – for example, the Slack integration it uses is removed, or its target type is no longer supported – PostHog automatically disables the subscription, records the change in the activity log, and emails the subscription owner. Re-enabling a subscription is blocked until the underlying issue is resolved. Disabled subscriptions are skipped by the delivery workflow, so they don't produce repeated failed deliveries.
+
 ## Testing subscriptions
 
 You can manually trigger a test delivery for any subscription. Click the **...** menu on a subscription in the list and select **Test delivery**. This immediately sends the subscription content to the configured target (email or Slack channel) without waiting for the next scheduled delivery.
 
 This is useful for verifying that the subscription is configured correctly and the content looks as expected.
+
+Test delivery is only available for enabled subscriptions. If a subscription was automatically disabled, resolve the underlying issue (such as reconnecting Slack) and re-enable it first.
